# ── Large binaries / installation archives (provided separately, never on GitHub) ──
# These files are downloaded on demand via apps/download-assets.sh
# (assets.links catalog). Do NOT commit them: they far exceed the
# GitHub repository limit (100 MB per file) and bloat the clone.
code/modules/Apps/ableton/**/*.zip
code/modules/Apps/davinci/*.zip
code/modules/Apps/spektrafilm/*.zip
code/modules/Apps/guitarpro/*.exe
code/modules/Apps/**/*.run
# Offline authorization files are machine-specific and never belong in git.
*.auz
code/modules/Apps/bitwig/*.deb
# Reapertips theme archive: collected from ~/Downloads by bootstrap.sh and kept
# local (it is not ours to redistribute). configs/custom/ IS committed: it is
# the config this repo ships.
code/modules/Apps/reaper/configs/*.zip
# Dated REAPER config backups stay local; the one-time Wayland migration
# backup (old X11 libSwell / imgui / launcher / hyprland.lua) IS committed.

# ── Local backups: copies made before an edit/install, never source ──
# A complete archive includes them only when the archive asks and the user
# accepts; git never does.
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.backup
*.backup.*
**/backups/
!code/modules/Apps/reaper/backups/
code/modules/Apps/reaper/backups/*
!code/modules/Apps/reaper/backups/2026-11-26_15-20-58-before-wayland-rewrite/

# ── Profile-owned Mixbay integrations (oscmix, evo-raw) ──
# Downloaded on demand by the interface profile that declares them, outside
# this checkout. If someone unpacks them here, they are still not source.
code/modules/mosquito/audio-stack/mixbay/integrations/

# ── Logs & transient install files ──
*.log
*.part

# update-desktop-database writes this next to whatever folder it is run from.
# A script that ran with this folder as CWD left one here; it is a cache, not
# part of the module, and mapping it to the "apps" module made the update
# screen propose a re-apply for a file nobody edited.
code/modules/Apps/mimeinfo.cache

# ── Crash logs: local-only, one dated log per failed mosquitOmarchy run ──
# Written by code/lib/crash.bash into .local/crash-logs/. NEVER pushed and
# NEVER archived (archive-customarchy.sh excludes .local/ too).
.local/

# ── Machine-scoped state (mosquito Audio Plugin Manager): per-machine, never committed ──# audio-plugin-manager-state.json is the installed-plugins truth log; the
# yabridge-driver.* pair is the same thing for the yabridge build/install
# bookkeeping the core writes next to itself (YABRIDGE_STATE / YABRIDGE_LOCK).
# All three describe THIS machine, and differ on every other one.
code/modules/mosquito/audio-stack/apm/audio-plugin-manager-state.json
code/modules/mosquito/audio-stack/apm/yabridge-driver.json
code/modules/mosquito/audio-stack/apm/yabridge-driver.lock

# ── Patches: scripts are tracked, local binaries/tools are not ──────────────
# Ableton's active patch scripts (PATCH/patch-ableton-wires.sh and
# wires/patch-move-wires.sh) ARE on GitHub: the TUI and setup-ableton-wires.sh call
# them. Menu repair is embedded in setup-ableton-wires.sh --fix-menu. The local-only
# extras are binaries, the venv, license files, abandoned experiments and the
# uninstall helper.
code/modules/Apps/ableton/wires/PATCH/tools/
code/modules/Apps/ableton/wires/PATCH/.venv/
code/modules/Apps/ableton/wires/PATCH/old/
code/modules/Apps/ableton/wires/PATCH/vcruntime140_1.dll
code/modules/Apps/ableton/wires/PATCH/uninstall-witchwand.sh
# Wires downloads/runtime are local payloads, never GitHub content.
code/modules/Apps/ableton/wires/wires/
code/modules/Apps/ableton/wires/*.tar.zst
code/modules/Apps/ableton/wires/*.sha256
code/modules/Apps/ableton/native/linux-native-ableton/
code/modules/Apps/ableton/native/PATCH/
code/modules/Apps/guitarpro/PATCH/
code/modules/Apps/davinci/PATCH/
code/modules/Apps/bitwig/PATCH/

# ── Python environments / caches for the patches ──
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ── Go build leftovers ──
# `go build ./...` inside a tui-go/ directory writes a binary named after that
# DIRECTORY ("tui-go"), and a bare `go build .` there drops a "tui-go" too. The
# two TUIs that ship a prebuilt binary keep their own tracked names
# (mosquitomarchy-tui, audio-plugin-manager-tui); jamjamjam-tui is built by
# setup-jamjamjam-plugin.sh from source and is deliberately NOT tracked.
# None of the "tui-go" files belong in the repo.
**/tui-go/tui-go
# `go build -C <dir> .` writes the binary as the DIRECTORY name, producing a
# file literally called "0" next to a main.go that sits in a directory called
# "tui-go" — the same artefact as above, from the same command.
**/tui-go/0
# A stray "0" in the repo ROOT has the same cause: `go build -C <dir> .` run
# from a shell whose working directory is the repo root writes the binary under
# the name of the directory, and a redirection that loses its target lands here.
# Keep it out of history rather than trying to remember which command does it.
/0
code/modules/mosquito/jamjamjam/tui-go/jamjamjam-tui
# A bare `go build .` in a directory whose main package is "live-mode-tui" also
# drops a binary with the PACKAGE name next to the real one. Only the
# mosquito-live-mode-tui name is deployed and tracked.
code/modules/mosquito/audio-stack/live-mode/tui-go/live-mode-tui

# ── Sensitive / never on a repository (even private) ──
# Authorization files (Ableton license), license-workaround tools
# (DaVinci patch-resolve.sh). Everything touching the patch stays local
# (and/or in the release archive).
code/modules/Apps/guitarpro/guitar-pro-8-licence.md

# ── Password files / archives: ultra-safety, NEVER in a repository ──
# KeePassXC databases and backup archives (the backups live in
# mosquitomarchy-backups/ next to the repo — this is a last-resort guard if
# one is ever copied elsewhere by mistake).
*.kdbx
*.kdbx.*
omarchy-backup-*.tar.gz
omarchy-backup-*.tar.gz.gpg
# The backups folder itself (created by the bootstrap next to the repo):
# machine archives must never be committed, the complete release type picks
# them up from disk instead.
mosquitomarchy-backups/

# ── User-only notes (see archive-customarchy.sh release) ──
SECRET-README.md
# Extracted DaVinci OFX plugin bundle (downloaded/manual)
code/modules/Apps/davinci/*.bundle/
code/modules/Apps/davinci/*.bundle

# `go test -cpuprofile` leaves the test binary behind in the package dir.
*.test

# Go build outputs: never tracked. The installers build these; a committed
# 27 MB binary goes stale and bloats every clone.
code/main tui/go/mosquitomarchy-tui
code/main tui/go/*.test
code/modules/**/tui-go/*-tui
code/modules/**/tui-go/*.test

# Addons are user-owned data. The shipped example emoticon is tracked; all
# other addons (scripts + images) stay local.
code/main tui/addons/*
!code/main tui/addons/emoticon/
!code/main tui/addons/emoticon/**
